---
/*
 * Deliberately NO `client:` directive — 18's re-examination of 07's ruling 9.
 *
 * 07 recorded this as "the one genuine island among the tag components", on the reading
 * that `<details>` open/close is client behaviour. It is not: `<details>`/`<summary>`
 * toggles natively, and everything the component adds on top is CSS — the "More ↓" /
 * "Less ↑" swap is `details[open] summary`, not state. `Expand.svelte` declares no
 * handler, no `$state` and no `$effect`; hydrating it changed nothing it rendered.
 *
 * What the island DID change was the layout, and only 16's computed-layout diff could
 * see it (finding 16-1). `<astro-island>` is `display: contents`, so it generates no box
 * — but CSS selectors match the DOM tree, so `article > *` landed on the island and
 * `<details>` fell through to auto-placement: on /about it computed `x843 w99`, one
 * column, in the row belonging to the paragraph above it, against `x269 w557`.
 *
 * Expand.svelte is the SvelteKit file, copied verbatim, and still is — it server-renders
 * through this wrapper exactly the way Gallery.svelte does.
 */
import Expand from '../lib/content/Expand.svelte'
---

<Expand><slot /></Expand>
